# Test conventions

## No network, no real data

All tests use **deterministic synthetic OHLCV** fixtures from `conftest.py`.
Never hit yfinance or any external service from a test. If you need a new
shape of price series, add a builder to `conftest.py`.

## Test scope per file

| File | Covers |
| --- | --- |
| `test_indicators.py` | EMA / RSI / MACD / ATR / ADX / Bollinger numerics |
| `test_signals.py` | 9 stock screener categories + score / confidence / trade plan |
| `test_regime.py` | Per-instrument regime classifier |
| `test_risk.py` | ATR%, volume, gap labels |
| `test_index_pivots.py` | Classical floor-trader pivots |
| `test_index_signals.py` | Index trend / breakout / pullback (LONG + SHORT) |
| `test_option_chain_metrics.py` | PCR, max-pain, IV-skew, bias, strike picker |
| `test_live_quotes.py` | Shared live-quote cache + Upstox / yfinance fallback |
| `test_live_verifier.py` | EOD signal verification status transitions |
| `test_live_movers.py` / `test_live_observer.py` / `test_live_strategy.py` / `test_live_regime.py` | Live Analysis engine pieces |

## Style

- Prefer pure-function tests over integration where possible.
- Use `pytest` parametrize for table-driven cases (multiple confidences,
  ATR%, setup types, etc.).
- Assert on **specific** values, not "is not None". The whole point of
  deterministic synthetic data is reproducibility.

## Run

```powershell
cd backend
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest -q
```

Add new tests in the right file; don't create a parallel `test_*_v2.py`.
